3. Data derived from OONI: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0

These files contain or are computed from measurements of the Open Observatory
of Network Interference (OONI), https://ooni.org. OONI publishes its data under
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, so these files are licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC-SA
4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode, with
attribution to OONI and to the authors.

- data/burn_units/derived/burn_units.csv
- data/burn_units/derived/burn_units_table.tex
- data/burn_units/derived/burn_units_evidence_long.csv
- data/burn_units/derived/ooni_cn_azurefd_daily.csv
- data/burn_units/derived/ooni_cn_monthly.csv
- data/burn_units/derived/ooni_platform_summary.csv
- data/burn_units/derived/ru_ooni_vs_registry.csv
- data/burn_units/derived/run_meta.json

No other data file of the repository is computed from OONI measurements. The
documentation quotes some values of the files above, with attribution to OONI.


4. Quoted passages and repeated third-party facts

Some files quote third-party papers, documentation pages, reports and commit
messages verbatim, to record where a value comes from. This holds for
data/literature/params_spec.py and data/minting/facts.py, for the quote checks
in the analysis scripts, and for the tables that carry the quotes:
data/literature/derived/params_table.csv,
data/literature/derived/quote_verification.csv,
data/minting/derived/doc_facts.csv,
data/snowflake/derived/churn_published.csv, the description column of
data/snowflake/derived/event_table.csv,
data/burn_units/derived/qualitative_events.csv, and the commit subjects in
data/snowflake/derived/summary.json and data/snowflake/raw/manifest.json.
These passages are cited excerpts. They keep the rights of their sources, and
the licenses above cover only the authors' selection, annotations and
computed values. data/minting/derived/psl_platform_suffixes.csv repeats rules
of the Public Suffix List, which is licensed MPL-2.0.
